## Cross-subject

All leans are to core courses in the same year. Math grade 7 and science grade 7 meet every school day, so their
course days are their school days (data/plans/calendar.csv); this course's day n falls in week n/2 rounded up.

### Mathematics, grade 7

| Row | Lean | Used here | Earliest math unit that teaches it | Bridge if math teaches it later |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| g7-design-with-variables | m7-proportional-tables (7.RP.A.2a: is one quantity proportional to another) | Unit 1, sessions 6 and 7 (weeks 3 and 4) | math grade 7 unit 2 (days 13 to 33, weeks 3 to 7) | The converter uses a given rate table and multiplies by its one rate, a grade 6 ratio move (6.RP); no proportional test is asked. If math's unit falls later, the reading-log design is the default and the converter an option |
| g7-pick-approach | m7-chance-probability (7.SP.C.5: probability as a number from 0 to 1) | Unit 4, sessions 34 and 35 (weeks 17 and 18) | math grade 7 unit 8 (days 139 to 157, weeks 28 to 32), later than this unit | The lunch-count problem is reasoned from patterns in past counts, in words (likely, unlikely); no probability number is used, so the session stands before math's unit |
| g7-viz-choices | m7-random-samples (7.SP.A.1: samples and populations) | Unit 3, sessions 25 and 26 (weeks 13 and 14) | math grade 7 unit 8 (days 139 to 157, weeks 28 to 32), later than this unit | The table is the whole data set, not a sample, and no claim about a population is made; mean and displays are grade 6 math (6.SP), so the unit stands before math's |

